  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The lotteries have distinct outcomes: Lottery A offers a sure outcome of 2400 Euros (100% probability). Lottery B offers 2500 Euros (33%), 2400 Euros (66%), and 0 Euros (1%). The reason focuses on the minimum absolute outcome, which is 0 Euros in Lottery B, and treats the sure outcome (2400 Euros) as a reference point. The differences between the sure outcome (2400) and the other outcomes (2500 and 0) are 100 and -2400, respectively. These differences are weighted by their probabilities (33% and 1%) in Lottery B, and the sum of the sure outcome and these weighted differences is computed. This process is mathematically defined and applicable to the given lotteries.",
